package main

import "strings"

// Help is a frozen reader overlay. It never changes a draft, recipient,
// permission selection or task state, and polling cannot retarget it.
func (m *console) openContextHelp() {
	title, body := "Workbench help", ""
	if m.nativeAction != nil {
		title = "Native delivery review help"
		body = "Shift+D configures how the selected native session receives broker-authorized turns. Manual keeps work in the inbox; Review requires an exact request approval; Auto delivers at a safe native boundary within the displayed turn, hop and cooldown limits. Instructions still require the sender's Commands permission. Notes and shared data remain observations. Unsupported or disconnected adapters cannot deliver automatically.\n\nArrow keys in this panel edit the displayed settings, not the global view. Enter first opens a final review; only Enter in that review applies it. The stable recipient and policy version are frozen. Failed submissions keep the exact draft. Ctrl-R reviews the current saved policy beside your retained choices; Enter there adopts only its version, without saving. Inspect the following final review before submitting again. Esc returns without submitting. Shift+A selects a pending request and opens its entire text before approving only that exact candidate. Human terminal drafts and native approvals are preserved."
	} else if m.teamAction != nil {
		title = "Review help"
		body = "This review freezes the selected identities and current version. Confirm only the displayed action. Esc returns without submitting. A conflict requires a fresh review; it never silently retargets an action. Invitations require the invited agent's consent. Removing an Agentmux-owned session can stop its descendant processes; disconnecting an external bridge leaves its original terminal running."
	} else if m.composer != "" {
		title = "Editor help · " + m.composer
		body = "Enter submits the displayed draft. Alt-Enter inserts a newline. Arrow keys move the cursor; Home/End move within a line, Ctrl-A/Ctrl-E to the whole draft's start/end. Ctrl-U clears. Esc cancels. Ctrl-G opens this help without changing the draft. Printable characters, including ?, remain literal text."
		switch m.composer {
		case "relaunch":
			body += "\n\nThe stable ID above is frozen. Enter with an empty selection deliberately starts a fresh native conversation. Type last to continue the provider's latest project conversation, picker to choose in its native UI, or an exact provider conversation ID. No history is guessed. The native CLI must have exited; healthy peer processes and the workspace attempt are preserved. After an uncertain response inspect sessions before trying again."
		case "send", "reply", "message":
			body += "\n\nThe intent above the editor is frozen for this draft. Ctrl-T switches between an informational note and an instruction task. Delivery is separate from permission: native sessions use Manual, Review or Auto under Sessions → Shift+D. Review requires approval of the exact request; Auto uses a supported native adapter at a safe boundary. Command permission alone does not wake a native session. Agentmux never types peer messages into your terminal editor. Notes remain observations and require their own delivery setting.\n\nReplies retain broker-validated ancestry. Every direct recipient must be able to see the referenced item; replies cannot widen the audience. A failed draft restores its original recipient, reference and intent with Ctrl-R from the workbench. Inspect possible delivery before retrying after transport errors."
		case "board":
			body += "\n\nThis is a shared informational note. The exact board namespace appears above the editor; a reply retains that board and structured ancestry. It never creates an instruction task. Different boards or private follow-ups require an explicit destination."
		case "memory-value":
			body += "\n\nMemory saves use the displayed namespace, key and CAS version. Ctrl-R reviews the latest saved value; Enter in that review adopts only its version, without saving. Review your retained draft before submitting. Private memory belongs to the selected authenticated agent. Imported source metadata is a claim, not authenticated identity."
		case "role":
			body += "\n\nRole changes use the exact session and role version captured when opening this editor. Native sessions receive an informational inbox notice and can query identity for the current role; no terminal input is injected. Managed workers capture the current role when claiming their next task. In-flight turns keep their existing input. If another editor changes the role, refresh and review before submitting your retained draft again."
		case "find":
			body = "Ctrl-P or / opens the same session switcher. Search task title, project, provider, stable ID or terminal location. Up/Down chooses a visible match; Enter opens its native terminal. Tab selects it in the current workbench without opening the terminal. In Teams, Tab also aligns the explicitly labeled team action target. Esc returns without changing the workbench selection. Existing terminals show their original terminal details where direct focus is unavailable. Exited native sessions open an explicit relaunch review. Polling cannot retarget a selected identity; if it disappears, choose again. Left/Right edits the query while this picker is open. Ctrl-G opens help without changing the query."
		default:
			if strings.HasPrefix(m.composer, "new-") {
				body += "\n\nA title is a human label. Choose coordinated to append Agentmux broker context and an optional role, or native-only to inject no prompt. Native Antigravity currently requires native-only; use the Pi bridge for injected coordination context. The provider's normal interactive tools and approvals remain available in local mode. A stable ID is generated independently of its title."
			}
		}
	} else {
		views := []struct{ title, body string }{
			{"Board", "[ / ] select a message, o reads its full text, r replies. A board reply retains its board; a direct reply retains the visible conversation. b posts to the selected board; +/- changes the board. s composes to the selected session. The editor shows note versus instruction intent before submission."},
			{"Sessions", "Up/Down selects a stable session ID. Enter opens the original native CLI for full interaction; F1 returns to this workbench. Shift+D configures Manual, Review or Auto native delivery, turn/hop limits and which observations can trigger a turn. Shift+A reviews the full text of an exact pending request before approval. Current mode, readiness, adapter capability and blocking reason appear in the status panel. Command permissions and native delivery are separate controls. When its process has exited, Enter opens a same-ID relaunch review instead; no automatic restart occurs. / searches and Shift+L renames the human task title. Shift+N creates a session. Shift+B edits admission reservations with a final CAS review (provider billing is not capped). x opens an exact frozen subtree review before revoking the session and its active descendants; an external bridge is disconnected without closing its native terminal."},
			{"Connections", "Up/Down selects the sender; h/l or Alt-Left/Alt-Right selects its recipient. m, p and i review note, ping and instruction permissions. c creates a scoped pair; d makes the sender independent across groups. Groups add independent contributions; explicit owner denies win. M/P/I remove an exact override. o shows effective-versus-stored sources. Existing accepted tasks are not cancelled by permission changes: review Tasks separately."},
			{"Memory", "Choose the displayed namespace before reading or editing. Effective read/write can differ from stored owner intent due to isolation, membership or ancestry. R resets an override without granting membership. n creates a key; v refreshes entries; e edits the selected value with its current CAS version. o reads full content and source claims. A conflict preserves the draft; Ctrl-R in the editor reviews the latest version without saving."},
			{"Tasks", "Select a task to inspect its delivery state, output and trace. PgDn loads older tasks; PgUp returns toward newer tasks. y filters the selected recipient and z cycles task states. Ctrl-K exposes exact versioned fail/retry recovery for uncertain tasks after you inspect side effects and stop the old process. f searches the complete task history by text, result or ID; an empty search clears the filter. o reads full owner-visible content; r creates a structured reply. Cancellation is explicit and can remain uncertain after transport loss. Inspect side effects before resolving or retrying; a new attempt is charged again."},
			{"Existing terminals", "Discovery is read-only: it inspects current-user process/terminal identities without reading prompts or credentials. c prepares a bridge. Paste its setup into the original native conversation yourself; Agentmux never injects setup or user turns. Observed IDs and registered session IDs are different."},
			{"Teams", "For everyday collaboration, press 3 for Connections, choose a recipient with h/l or Alt-Left/Alt-Right, then c to connect a pair. Those owner groups provide a scoped board and memory. This Teams view shows dynamic teams created by agents with configured permission. Invitations require the invited agent's own acceptance. The available keys follow the selected team, target membership and connection state. e edits name/description; t proposes a current member as owner. Ownership changes only after that agent accepts using its own credential. Lifetime allocations are not refunded when a team dissolves."},
			{"Events", "Inspect lifecycle and policy events alongside the current task state. Shift-F searches complete event history; g scopes it to the selected session; PgUp/PgDn pages history. An explicitly selected event remains pinned through polling until Home returns to live newest events. Polling does not imply a model is active. Research controls pause/resume/step/stop the study runner, while native terminal interaction remains separate. An offline observer never grants authority to mutate state."},
		}
		index := m.tab
		if index < 0 || index >= len(views) {
			index = 0
		}
		title, body = views[index].title+" help", views[index].body
		body += "\n\nCtrl-K opens searchable executable Actions with exact targets, shortcuts and unavailable reasons. Shift-N inherits provider and project: Enter reviews an optional title, then Enter launches. Ctrl-O from the title opens advanced configuration. Actions also exposes exact group disable, global isolation impact, retired-session cleanup, knowledge exposure and whole-study follow/details. Ctrl-W opens Workspaces while keeping the current draft or review intact; an owned attachment hands its foreground client across servers and restores the same private dashboard on return.\n\nCtrl-P or / opens the searchable session switcher: arrows choose, Enter opens the native terminal, Tab selects here, Esc returns. Session titles, stable IDs, providers and projects distinguish similar sessions. In the session sidebar, Up/Down changes the selected session; Connections labels it as the sender and labels the independently selected recipient.\n\nLeft/Right switches between all eight views, including Connections and Teams. Ctrl-Left/Ctrl-Right is an alias. In Connections and Teams, h/l or Alt-Left/Alt-Right selects the recipient or action target. Up/Down selects an agent or observed terminal. Tab/Shift-Tab also switches views; 1–8 selects one directly. While editing, reviewing or reading, arrow keys stay inside that open panel.\n\nUppercase shortcuts mean hold Shift: Shift+N starts a session, Shift+L edits its title, Shift+V edits its coordinated role, Shift+U reviews a relaunch, and Shift+W chooses a workspace. The footer lists actions for this view and selection. ? opens context help; Esc returns. q detaches/closes the observer while sessions keep running. Titles may repeat; operations use the stable IDs shown with them.\n\nIn an owned attachment, the workspace chooser hands off that attachment; use the chooser again to return to the previous workspace and its preserved dashboard. A standalone observer opens another observer; q returns to the previous one. When native input needs another tmux server, the standalone observer shows the exact attach command for a separate terminal. Every workspace action targets its selected state directory."
	}
	m.reader = &consoleReader{title: title, body: body, help: true}
}
